  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Number of persons trained (border security &amp; CSOs) trained on SALW control and the critical role of women for sensitization.
- No of communities reached with sensitization and awareness campaigns conducted by the project per region based on communication strategy and focused on women and community groups.
- No of people (disaggregated by gender) reached with sensitization and awareness campaigns based on communication strategy and focused on women and community groups</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">0</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conduct a Mapping Study of donor intervention on SALW in fifteen (15) ECOWAS Member States in collaboration with ECOWAS, National Commissions on SALW and UNDP.
Organize and Conduct Ballot without Bullets sensitization campaign to forestall Election Violence.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conducted mapping study of donor intervention on key thematic areas in fifteen ECOWAS Member States.
Conducted two validation meeting with all ECOWAS member states represented by NATCOMs in Niamey and Monrovia to validate the preliminary results of Regional SALW Mapping exercise.
Published mapping report in English and translated to French.
Developed an interactive platform/database analytics on Power BI to provides an in-depth analysis of weapons and ammunition management
Conducted a Ballot without Bullet sensitization campaign across the country which resulted in almost zero incidences of armed violence in critical flashpoints before, during and after the elections in Ghana</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provide technical /operational capacity to set up cross border security structure at 3 selected border communities for enhance border security coordination .</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Established and set up 3 Cross Border Security coordination structure at border communities of Elubo (Ghana) Noe (Cote dIvoire, and Dakola ( Burkina Faso)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provide technical /operational capacity to decentralize NATCOMS to facilitate the setup of decentralized units in selected border communities.
Support the NatCom to set up Violence platform through a data collection system for reporting armed violence.
Build Capacity of Civil Society Organizations (CSOs) on emerging trends of SALW to lead advocacy.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support NatCom to set up 3 decentralize offices in Cote Ivoire and delivered equipment to support the operations of the decentralized offices at the border communities.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
